## California Lemon Law and Used Vehicles

The California lemon law extends to used vehicles, but with a few conditions.

Dealership Warranty

Many dealerships in California offer warranties on used vehicles, typically covering 30 days after purchase or the first 1,000 miles on the odometer, whichever comes first. If your used vehicle develops significant issues within this warranty - and meets the requirements of Santa Rosa lemon law - it could be treated like a new vehicle when filing a claim.

## Your Santa Rosa Lemon Law Rights

Under California’s lemon law, dealerships are obligated to either repair the faulty vehicle or provide a buyback option if the vehicle qualifies as a lemon. The warrantor is responsible for covering your legal expenses.

Did You Buy the Vehicle “As Is”?

When you buy a vehicle “as is,” you accept responsibility for any existing defects, which means you may not be eligible for protection under California lemon law. These terms must be clearly outlined in the buyer’s guide while the vehicle is on display. If the dealership fails to disclose this, you could still file for compensation - a skilled lemon law attorney in Santa Rosa can help you manage the process.

